{"id":31136,"path":"/grammar-points/shorts/say-vs-tell-grammar-shorts/","parentId":30685,"order":1920,"section":"grammar-points","level":null,"depth":3,"title":"Say vs Tell – Grammar Shorts","seo":{"title":"Say vs Tell – Grammar Shorts - Test-English","description":"Learn the difference between 'say' and 'tell' and how to use them correctly with our short grammar lesson with a grammar chart and an exercise","image":"/media/uploads/Say-vs-tell_Grammar-shorts.webp"},"modified":"2025-06-04T16:11:08","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>Say vs Tell</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-31166\" src=\"/media/uploads/Say-vs-Tell_Grammar-chart.webp\" alt=\"Grammar chart illustrating the difference between 'say' and 'tell' with examples and special expressions.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <p>Let’s learn the difference between the verbs <strong>say</strong> and <strong>tell</strong>. These verbs have similar meanings but are used in different ways.</p> <h3>Tell SOMEONE</h3> <p>After the verb <strong>tell</strong>, we always need an indirect object (the person we are telling).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I always <span><strong>tell him</strong></span> I love him.</em></li> <li><em>The teacher <span><strong>told us</strong></span> to leave.</em></li> </ul> <h4>Exceptions</h4> <p>We can use&nbsp;<strong>tell</strong> without a personal object (<strong>me, your, him, her, etc.</strong>) with some expressions: <strong>tell a story, tell the time, tell a lie, tell the truth, tell a secret, tell a joke, tell the difference.</strong></p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>You must <span><strong>tell the truth</strong></span>. <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li>You must <span><strong>tell us the truth</strong></span>. <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li>You must&nbsp;<span><strong>say the truth</strong></span>. <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h3>Say SOMETHING</h3> <p>After the verb <strong>say</strong>, we need a direct object (the thing that is said).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>says that</strong></span> she is happy.</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>said <span>something</span></strong></span>.</em></li> </ul> <p>If you want to include the indirect object, you need to add <strong>to</strong> before the person.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She said <span><strong>to me</strong></span> that she was happy.</em></li> <li><em>She said something <span><strong>to Clara</strong></span>.</em></li> </ul> <h3>Common mistakes!</h3> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>said me</strong></span> that she was happy. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>told me</strong></span> that she was happy. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>said&nbsp;that</strong></span> she was happy. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>told that</strong></span> everything was OK. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>said that</strong></span> everything was OK. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <div class=\"grammar-separator-dots\"><span>Take the Quiz!</span></div> <div data-quiz=\"1202\"></div>"],"explanation":null,"quizzes":[{"id":1202,"questions":[{"id":10259,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She _____ me she was moving to a new city.</div>","choices":[{"id":18697,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18698,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10260,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He _____ he didn't like the movie.</div>","choices":[{"id":18699,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18700,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10261,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Can you _____ me what time it is?</div>","choices":[{"id":18701,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>say</span>"},{"id":18702,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>tell</span>"}]},{"id":10262,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They _____ they would arrive by noon.</div>","choices":[{"id":18703,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18704,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10263,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Did she _____ you about the meeting?</div>","choices":[{"id":18705,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>say</span>"},{"id":18706,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>tell</span>"}]},{"id":10268,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She _____ to us that she was feeling better.</div>","choices":[{"id":18715,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18716,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10264,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He _____ the truth during the interview.</div>","choices":[{"id":18707,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18708,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10265,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Please _____ something nice to her.</div>","choices":[{"id":18709,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>say</span>"},{"id":18710,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>tell</span>"}]},{"id":10266,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ her to be careful on the trip.</div>","choices":[{"id":18711,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18712,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]},{"id":10267,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The teacher _____ the class to be quiet.</div>","choices":[{"id":18713,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>said</span>"},{"id":18714,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>told</span>"}]}]}]}